The `.tab-view` has `display: none` when inactive and `display: block` when `.active`. CSS transitions cannot animate from `display: none` to `display: block` — the opacity/transform transition never fires. The element just pops in.

This is a known limitation. Add `animation` to the active state to provide a visual transition instead.

Change:
```
.tab-view.active {
  display: block;
  opacity: 1;
  transform: translateY(0);
}
```
to:
